s.\n\nBest discard is likely W6, as it's the most isolated and doesn't contribute to potential melds. After discarding W6, my hand becomes more focused on T and B, with J1 pair. I can then draw tiles to form chows or pungs.\n\nReason: W6 is a lone tile with no connections, and discarding it improves hand shape without sacrificing potential sequences or pairs. Keeping pairs (J1, T1, T6, B6) is important for flexibility. The F4 pung already gives good points, so I need to build the rest of the hand efficiently. W6 is also relatively safe based on discard history.\n\nAnswer: Play W6"}
